OpenStax's source MathML for one exercise glues the minus sign and the pi
symbol together into a single <mo>–π</mo> node, so the converter cannot map
the two symbols individually. The cumulative patch restores that expression
and also records the manual mathematical and typographic review: set-builder
notation, operator semantics, punctuation and math-mode boundaries, piecewise
densities, and accessibility descriptions are corrected. In particular, the
figure whose boundaries are x = ±pi/3 no longer describes them as x = ±1,
and the Alhazen-lunes description consistently names diameters AB and BC.
All blank and whitespace-only lines are preserved exactly.

